WEBVTT

00:00.150 --> 00:01.225
The Southern Cross.

00:01.925 --> 00:06.452
The smallest of the eighty-eight constellations, and the best known south of the equator.

00:06.990 --> 00:11.185
Five countries fly it on their flags, Australia and Brazil among them.

00:11.612 --> 00:17.707
The nearer of the two bright stars beside it is Alpha Centauri, the closest star system to the Sun.

00:18.307 --> 00:24.449
The dark patch at its foot is the head of the Emu that Aboriginal Australians see in the Milky Way.
